   "fix": "Add `@[simp] theorem coe_mk (f : V \u2192 V \u2192 G) (h\u2081) (h\u2082) : \u21d1(\u27e8f, h\u2081, h\u2082\u27e9 : GaugeLink V G) = f := (rfl)` next to `toFun_eq_coe`.",
   "issue": "`toFun_eq_coe` (`W.toFun = W`, `@[simp]`) is the only coercion lemma; there is no `coe_mk`/`mk_apply`. Since simp rewrites `W.toFun \u2192 \u21d1W`, a goal `(\u27e8f, h\u2081, h\u2082\u27e9 : GaugeLink V G) x y = f x y` is unreachable by `simp` and only closes by defeq. The module docstring advertises constructing new links from the two fields as the intended extension point, so this is the form consumers will hit.",
